  authorization_consistency:
    verdict: INCONSISTENT
    detail: |-
      17 mutating endpoints gated by SECURITY_RULES (DATA_ENTITY_*); 27+ read
      endpoints fall through to .authenticated() with no role/owner gate; DATA_ENTITY_ADD_TERM
      and DATA_ENTITY_DELETE_TERM rules silently disabled by `/term` vs `/terms` path
      mismatch (SecurityConstants.java:237-242 vs DataEntityApi.java:148, 542); attachment
      chunk path gate authorises against URL's data_entity_id but file lands against
      uploadId's originating entity (cross-entity hijack); Activity feed cross-owner
      exposure repeats the same admin-path-without-admin-gate failure mode. **Batch
      H confirms at the SQL primary source**: ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl has
      NO authorization annotation at the repository layer (every method signature
      lacks principal/owner parameter; ReactiveDataEntityRepository.java:1-119 interface
      confirms). The repository trusts upstream controller-layer authorization gates
      with NO defence-in-depth.
  owner_scoping:
    verdict: MIXED
    detail: 'Owner-scoped: `/my`, `/my/upstream`, `/my/downstream` (delegated to reactor
      Context). Bypasses owner: `/popular`, `getDataEntityDetails`, `getDataEntityActivity`,
      `getDataEntityMessages`, lineage reads, DEG children/items/lineage, global Activity
      feed (ALL/UPSTREAM/DOWNSTREAM type-dispatch paths), Slack-message posting (cross-owner
      posting accepted). Mutations gated per-resource by DATA_ENTITY policy resolver.
      Directory non-owner-scoped catalog-wide view. **Batch H SQL primary source confirms
      BYPASSES at JOIN time**: every list-shape method on the repository (listPopular,
      findByState, getDimensions, getDetails, getQuerySuggestions, listByOddrns) returns
      rows with NO per-tenant filter at the SQL layer; owner-scoping is the CALLER''s
      responsibility (listByOwner accepts ownerId as parameter; the repository does
      NOT verify the caller IS that owner).'
  strengths:
  - Mutating endpoints centralised in SECURITY_RULES with DATA_ENTITY policy context
    (SecurityConstants.java:194-324)
  - DATA_ENTITY policy resolver evaluates user policies against resource owner/namespace/datasource/class/type
  - Per-resource permission model exists (Permissions / Roles / Owners / User-owner
    association per ODD vocabulary)
  - '**Audit-log emission CONFIRMED for DataEntity mutations (batch F POSITIVE FINDING)**
    — `updateStatus` emits `DATA_ENTITY_STATUS_UPDATED` activity events with explicit
    `oldState` + `newState` payloads (programmatic, NOT AOP `@ActivityLog`); `createOwnership`
    emits `OWNERSHIP_CREATED` via `@ActivityLog` on OwnershipServiceImpl.create. DataEntity
    mutations are TIER-1 AUDITED — contrast with TIER-2 RBAC mutations (Role/Policy/Owner)
    which have NO audit. The platform has a 2-tier audit story; this concept is on
    the audited side. (updateStatus.md:implicit_adrs.[4] + createOwnership.md:implicit_adrs.[1])'
  - '**Hollow-entities unconditionally shielded from CTE-based lists (batch H SQL primary
    source)** — cteDataEntitySelect line 918 applies HOLLOW.isFalse() in every list-shape
    query; the only escape hatches are raw get() and listByOddrns(..., includeHollow=true).
    Hollow rows (ingestion placeholders) carry exclude_from_search=true from birth
    (buildHollowRecord lines 862-864) — dual-flagged. The defence-in-depth shielding
    keeps ingestion-placeholder rows away from user-facing surfaces.'
  weaknesses:
  - DATA_ENTITY_ADD_TERM and DATA_ENTITY_DELETE_TERM gates SILENTLY DISABLED by `/term`
    (SecurityConstants.java:237-242) vs `/terms` (DataEntityApi.java:148, 542) path
    mismatch — any authenticated user can attach/detach terms on any entity
  - All 27+ read endpoints (`getDataEntityDetails`, `getDataEntityAlerts`, `getDataEntityMessages`,
    `getDataEntityActivity`, `getDataEntityMetrics`, lineage reads) carry no role/owner/permission
    gate — auth-mode-only reads of every entity's full payload
  - '**CENTERPIECE READ CROSS-OWNER EXPOSURE (batch F — RESOLVES ADR-CANDIDATE-003
    borderline_flag as INTENTIONAL DELIBERATE posture)** — `getDataEntityDetails`
    (`GET /api/dataentities/{id}`) is the single hottest endpoint on the platform;
    any authenticated user (any anonymous caller under DISABLED) receives the FULL
    34-field DataEntityDetails payload — ownership[] list, internalDescription, externalDescription,
    tags[], terms[], metadataFieldValues[], dataSource, linkedUrlList[], viewCount,
    isStale, sourceList[]/targetList[]/outputList[]/inputList[], including SOFT-DELETED
    entities (`includeDeleted(true)` is deliberate). 4th read-collaborative cross-owner-enumeration
    surface — WIDEST blast radius (the platform''s primary UI read). The doc-gap is
    that live `/configuration-and-deployment/enable-security/authorization` does NOT
    name this posture. (getDataEntityDetails.md:security.known_security_gaps.[0] severity
    HIGH; bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[0])'
  - '**Read-as-write `view_count` increment on every GET (batch F)** — `getDataEntityDetails`
    UPDATE-s `data_entity.view_count` inside `@ReactiveTransactional` on every successful
    read. Unauthenticated under DISABLED → any caller can inflate any entity''s `view_count`
    arbitrarily to push it to the top of `getPopular` ranking. Hot-key contention
    on the platform''s most-popular entities. No idempotency, no rate-limit, no debouncing.
    (getDataEntityDetails.md:security.known_security_gaps.[3] severity MEDIUM; performance.known_performance_gaps.[0]).
    **Batch H SQL primary source confirms**: incrementViewCount at ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.java:173-180
    is bare UPDATE ... view_count = view_count + 1 with no rate limit and no per-caller
    throttle.'
  - '`getDataEntityActivity` exposes who-changed-what audit trail to any authenticated
    user'
  - '`getDataEntityMessages` exposes Slack-thread content to any authenticated user
    (cross-tenant exposure if Slack workspace has multiple sensitive channels)'
  - Global `/api/activity` returns audit trails across every owner — including ActivityState
    old/new diffs of descriptions, business names, ownership changes, custom metadata
    — to ANY authenticated user (getActivity.md:security.known_security_gaps.[0] severity
    HIGH)
  - '**Catalog-wide search enumeration (batch E)** — `POST /api/search` + paginated
    `GET /api/search/{search_id}/results` enumerates every non-EXCLUDE_FROM_SEARCH
    Data Entity in the platform with no owner predicate to ANY authenticated user.
    Same admin-path-without-admin-gate failure mode as getAllAlerts / getActivity
    but WIDER blast radius (the search surface is the platform''s primary catalog
    discovery vector). search.md:security.known_security_gaps.[0] severity HIGH'
  - '**Lineage-graph cross-owner enumeration (batch F)** — `GET /api/dataentities/{id}/lineage/downstream`
    (sibling `/upstream`) returns the FULL reachable lineage subgraph from any rooted
    entity, including entities owned by other teams. Lineage edges encode causal connections
    — leaking the existence of a downstream transformer or consumer reveals another
    team''s internal pipeline structure even if their individual entities are not
    separately enumerable. Wider than alerts/activity/search because graphs traverse
    owner boundaries. Combined with no `lineage_depth` upper-bound cap and no CTE
    cycle guard, this is also a DoS-amplification vector. (getDataEntityDownstreamLineage.md:security.known_security_gaps.[0,1]
    severity HIGH)'
  - Slack-message posting accepts any user-supplied data_entity_id with no owner check
    — cross-tenant message injection (postMessageInSlack.md:security.known_security_gaps.[2]
    severity HIGH)
  - 'Attachment chunk hijack: caller with DATA_ENTITY_ATTACHMENT_MANAGE on entity
    X who learns another user''s uploadId for entity Z can post chunks via X''s URL
    — gate authorises path entity, service forwards to uploadId entity (uploadFileChunk.md:security.known_security_gaps.[0]
    severity MEDIUM)'
  - '**Owner-auto-create permission-bypass via createOwnership (batch F)** — `POST
    /api/dataentities/{id}/ownership` calls `OwnerService.getOrCreate(owner_name)`
    which silently creates a fresh `OwnerPojo` when the name is novel. Any caller
    with `DATA_ENTITY_OWNERSHIP_CREATE` can mint new Owner directory entries WITHOUT
    holding `OWNER_CREATE` permission. Same auto-create pattern on Title (`title_name`
    becomes a Title directory row with no allowlist, no length cap, no audit). Structural
    permission-escalation surface: the documented `OWNER_CREATE` permission gate on
    `POST /api/owners` is incomplete — this endpoint is a second write path into the
    Owner directory. (createOwnership.md:security.known_security_gaps.[0] + bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[0,1]
    severity MEDIUM)'
  - '**Status-update self-grant ambiguity + cross-tenant assignment (batch F)** —
    `createOwnership` accepts any caller-supplied `owner_name` (including names that
    don''t correspond to the caller). A Policy granting `DATA_ENTITY_OWNERSHIP_CREATE`
    without `"is": "dataEntity:owner"` condition is functionally root on any entity''s
    ownership; the docs do not enumerate default Policies. Self-grant feasibility
    undocumented. (createOwnership.md:bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[6,7] severity
    MEDIUM)'
  - Authorization layer is path-string-coupled with no compile-time/test-time guard
    against drift; the term mismatch is the canonical example, no integration test
    currently catches such drift
  - Attachment subsystem (a per-entity feature) has its own systemic security weaknesses
    — see Attachment concept's security_aggregate
  - Under auth.type=DISABLED, every endpoint becomes anonymously reachable — now 12-SIDECAR
    triangulated; ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl (batch H) joins the 11 prior sidecars
    as the SQL-layer confirmation that the persistence layer has no auth check whatsoever.
  - '**NEW BATCH H — SQL-injection vector in getHighlightedResult (HIGH)** — ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.java:799-806
    builds raw SQL via `String.formatted(text, tsQuery)` and passes the resulting
    string to `DSL.field(sql, String.class)`. The `text` parameter is the server-assembled
    `searchableString` from DataEntityHighlightConverter.convert(...) which includes
    user-controllable fields (`internal_name`, `internal_description`, tags). The
    `query` parameter passes through JooqFTSHelper.tsQuery which only does prefix-matching,
    NOT escaping. A user-writable `internal_description` containing `'); DROP TABLE
    data_entity; --` would land verbatim into the `text` slot of `ts_headline(''english'',
    ''%s'', ...)`, breaking out of the SQL string literal. Attack surface gated by
    DATA_ENTITY_DESCRIPTION_UPDATE (writer-side) + DATA_ENTITY_VIEW (reader-side)
    — both bypassed under auth.type=DISABLED. This is the only raw-SQL-format path
    in the 982-line file. (ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.md:bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[0]
    + security.known_security_gaps.[0])'
  - '**NEW BATCH H — REFACTOR-222 confirmed at SQL primary source (MEDIUM)** — `cteDataEntitySelect`
    helper (lines 909-939) is the CTE-builder consumed by 9 list-shape methods (`listPopular`,
    `listByOwner`, `listByTerm`, `getDEGExperimentRuns`, `getDimensions(id|oddrns|ids)`,
    `getDetails(id)`, `getQuerySuggestions`) and OMITS `EXCLUDE_FROM_SEARCH.isFalse()`.
    Other paths route through `getDataEntityDefaultConditions` (lines 970-976) which
    DOES apply the filter — `countByState`, `countByDatasourceAndType`, `getDataSourceEntityTypeIds`,
    `getCountByDataSources`, `getDataEntityDomainsInfo`, `getDataEntityWithOwnership`.
    `findByState` re-adds the predicate via `JooqFTSHelper.resultFacetStateConditions`
    line 149, so it IS filtered. The inconsistency means entities flagged exclude_from_search=true
    ARE included in popular / my-objects / by-term / by-DEG / details / suggestions;
    NOT included in count-by-state, statistics, search facet, count-by-datasource.
    (ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.md:bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[1])'
  cross_file_inconsistencies:
  - DataEntityController and DataEntityAttachmentController both authorize via SECURITY_RULES
