  throughput_shape:
    verdict: SINGLE_ITEM_ONLY
    detail: All 40 mutating endpoints take a single dataEntityId path variable; no
      bulk-update endpoint for description/name/status/ownership/tags/terms/metadata/alert
      config. Bulk operator workflows (tag-namespace, status-batch) require N round-trips.
      Per-chunk upload is single-chunk-per-request (no batch chunk endpoint). Activity
      feed is single-window per call (no batch / multi-window endpoint).
  scaling_shape:
    verdict: UNPAGINATED
    detail: Lineage endpoints unbounded `lineageDepth` + unbounded `expandedEntityIds`.
      Page/Size pagination required but unconstrained at controller (no @Max). Directory
      landing has no pagination on type-card list. `getDataEntityClasses`/`getDomains`/`getDataEntitiesUsage`
      are platform-wide aggregates with no caching. Activity feed `size` parameter
      unbounded (no @Max). Attachment chunk staging keyed only by uploadId (per-instance
      local filesystem) regardless of attachment.storage mode. **Batch H confirms
      pagination as `(page-1)*size`** at ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.java:632
      and 6 other paginated list methods — caller passing page=0 produces negative
      offset → Postgres 500 error; no `validatePage(int page)` utility enforcing page
      >= 1.
  strengths:
  - All 40 endpoints reactive Mono<ResponseEntity<...>> — non-blocking I/O, request
    thread released during DB await (DataEntityController.java:84-453)
  - Stateless controller — instances scale horizontally; no in-memory state, no locking,
    no advisory locks (DataEntityController.java:71-81)
  - Activity stream uses cursor pagination (`lastEventId` + `lastEventDateTime`) —
    appropriate for append-only audit data, avoids deep-offset cliffs (DataEntityController.java:351-365
    + ActivityController.java:34-35)
  - '**Batch H — single-statement CTE assembly via cteDataEntitySelect helper** —
    every list-shape method uses ONE CTE-builder helper (lines 909-939) layered with
    DataEntityCTEQueryConfig per call site; one round-trip per list, no N+1 fan-out;
    jsonArrayAgg over aggregated relations (owners/titles/ownership/tags/metadata)
    keeps the entire detail assembly in one query (lines 295-304, 768-797, 880-887).'
  weaknesses:
  - No upper bound on pagination `size` parameter at the controller — caller can pass
    `size=2147483647` per spec (components.yaml:4213-4229)
  - No max-depth bound on lineage endpoints; `lineageDepth=1000000` reaches LineageService
    unmodified (DataEntityController.java:256-273)
  - '**Batch F primary-source detailed**: NO `@Min(1)` lower bound enforced via `@Min(1)`
    on the generated `DataEntityApi` but NO `@Max(...)` upper bound. Missing `lineage_depth`
    causes null-Integer NPE on autoboxing to primitive `int` at LineageService boundary
    — docs claim ''Unset returns the platform''s default depth'' which is UNIMPLEMENTED.
    `expanded_entity_ids` has no `maxItems` cap — exceeds Postgres 32K-parameter prepared-statement
    limit silently. (getDataEntityDownstreamLineage.md:bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[0-2]
    severity HIGH)'
  - '**No CTE cycle guard on lineage recursion (batch F)** — `UNION ALL` body without
    visited-set; only termination is `tDepth.lessThan(lineageDepth.getDepth())`. Diamond-shaped
    DAGs amplify intermediate rows before outer `selectDistinct` deduplication. (getDataEntityDownstreamLineage.md:bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[3,7]
    severity MEDIUM)'
  - '**View-count UPDATE on hottest read is write-bound under load (batch F primary-source)**
    — `data_entity.view_count` is row-locked O(reads); popular entities become write-throughput
    bottlenecks; defeats Postgres read replicas (the endpoint is permanently primary-only
    at the DB layer). Mitigation options unimplemented: async batch increment, sample-and-aggregate,
    separate counter table. (getDataEntityDetails.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[0]
    severity MEDIUM)'
  - '**~10 DB round-trips per detail-page render with NO caching (batch F primary-source)**
    — the most-used endpoint is also the most DB-intensive read in the system. Caffeine
    cache keyed by `dataEntityId` with short TTL + invalidation on mutation endpoints
    would cut detail-page DB load by ~90% for repeated views. (getDataEntityDetails.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[1]
    severity MEDIUM)'
  - '**No HTTP cache headers on getDataEntityDetails (batch F)** — every refresh re-transfers
    the full 34-field payload AND triggers a view-count UPDATE. ETag derived from
    `(updated_at, view_count)` + `Cache-Control: max-age=10` would handle browser
    304s. (getDataEntityDetails.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[2] severity
    LOW)'
  - '**Unbounded `entities[]`/`sourceList[]`/`targetList[]`/`outputList[]`/`inputList[]`/`datasetsList[]`
    lineage-shortcut arrays in DataEntityDetails response (batch F)** — a DEG with
    10K children produces a 10K-row response. No paging, no truncation, no `@Size(max=...)`
    constraint. (getDataEntityDetails.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[3] severity
    LOW)'
  - No caching on platform-wide aggregates `getDataEntityClasses` / `getDomains` /
    `getDataEntitiesUsage`
  - No `@Timed` / Micrometer / structured logging at the controller layer — latency
    regressions invisible at controller boundary
  - 'No bulk-operation endpoints for any per-entity attribute — UI bulk workflows
    pay N round-trips (batch F: updateStatus single-id only — no bulk status-change
    endpoint covering arbitrary entity lists; propagate=true only helps when batch
    is exactly a DEG''s children)'
  - '**updateStatus DEG-propagation transaction has no member-count cap (batch F)**
    — a 10K-member DEG transition runs the full cascade (lineage / group-relations
    / parent-group-relations / statistics / filled-flag) inside ONE `@ReactiveTransactional`
    boundary. Lock acquisition fan-out scales linearly with member count. Scheduled
    `DataEntityStatusSwitchJob` also has no per-tick batch cap. (updateStatus.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[1,2]
    severity MEDIUM)'
  - Directory landing page loads all data sources unfiltered into memory (DirectoryServiceImpl.java:48-50)
    — O(N) memory + parsing on every hit
  - Reflection-based ODDRN-property extraction in Directory is unmemoised (DirectoryServiceImpl.java:153-171)
  - Multi-instance attachment chunk staging broken for BOTH LOCAL and REMOTE storage
    backends — chunk path /tmp/odd/chunks is hardcoded, not config-driven (uploadFileChunk.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[0])
  - Activity counts endpoint issues 4 parallel aggregation queries per call — 4x DB
    load on every counts refresh (getActivity.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[1])
  - Search endpoint runs unconditional `my_objects` aggregation cost on every call
    — even when caller's SearchFormData.my_objects=false the owner-scoped countByState(state,
    owner) still runs to populate the UI's 'My objects' badge count. A short-circuit
    would halve per-call DB work in the common case (search.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[0])
  - '**NEW BATCH H — No index on data_entity.view_count (MEDIUM)** — `listPopular`
    issues `ORDER BY view_count DESC` (ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.java:633)
    against `data_entity`; the migration audit found NO `view_count` index in any
    of 91 migration files. For 100K+ entity catalogs this degrades linearly to full
    table scan + sort. The small LIMIT (typically 5-20) lets Postgres use a top-N
    sort, but the lack of index is a known scaling hazard. (ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[0])'
  - '**NEW BATCH H — 7-LEFT-JOIN fan-out on `getDataEntitySearchFields` (LOW)** —
    lines 768-797 join OWNERSHIP / OWNER / TITLE / TAG_TO_DATA_ENTITY / TAG / METADATA_FIELD_VALUE
    / METADATA_FIELD on a single root row; for entities with many tags + many metadata
    + many owners, query-plan cost grows multiplicatively. Mapper-side dedup is required
    on jsonArrayAgg over a fan-out to avoid N×M duplicates inside the JSON arrays
    (not verified in batch H — pending integration test). (ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.md:performance.known_performance_gaps.[2]
    + bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[7])'
  - '**NEW BATCH H — Pagination `(page-1)*size` does NOT validate page >= 1 across
    7 list methods (LOW)** — listPopular (line 632), listByOddrns (line 250), listByOwner
    (line 530), findByState (line 722), getDimensions (line 390), getDEGEntities/Experiment
    (lines 530, 589), getQuerySuggestions (variants). A page=0 caller produces negative
    offset; Postgres rejects with a 500 error. A single `validatePage(int page)` utility
    would close 7 occurrences. (ReactiveDataEntityRepositoryImpl.md:bugs_limitations_corner_cases.[5])'
  - Activity stream uses cursor pagination; everything else uses offset pagination
    — single inconsistent shape across the controller's 40 endpoints
  - Directory carries platform-wide aggregates without pagination; DataEntityController
    list endpoints carry pagination but no caps — different unscoped patterns for
    the same Data Entity concept
  - Chunk staging path /tmp/odd/chunks is the same for LOCAL and REMOTE storage; class-level
    Attachment sidecar identified LOCAL multi-instance risk, method-level uploadFileChunk
    sidecar reveals it's storage-mode-independent
